{
  "id": "most-stones-removed-same-row-column",
  "questionId": "most-stones-removed-same-row-column",
  "slug": "most-stones-removed-same-row-column",
  "title": "Most Stones Removed with Same Row or Column",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Union find",
  "patterns": [
    "union find",
    "connected components"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "within a connected group of stones, you can always remove all but one - so the answer is total stones minus number of connected groups",
    "you don't need to compare every pair of stones directly - union each stone with a shared 'row bucket' and 'column bucket' node instead",
    "encode row x as one union-find id and column y as a different union-find id (for example, offset column ids so they never collide with row ids), then union each stone's row id with its column id",
    "count the number of distinct roots among only the stone nodes at the end, then subtract from stones.length"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "comparing every pair of stones directly (O(n^2) unions) instead of using shared row/column ids as bridge nodes",
    "letting row and column ids collide because they weren't offset into separate ranges",
    "counting the row/column bridge nodes themselves as if they were stone components"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given the positions of stones on an infinite 2D plane, where each stone is a pair `[x, y]`. No two stones share the same position. You may remove a stone if it shares a row or a column with some other stone that is still on the board.\n\n**Return the maximum number of stones you can remove.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= stones.length <= 1000",
      "0 <= x, y <= 10000",
      "no two stones share the same [x, y] position"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a single stone (nothing to remove)",
      "every stone isolated - no two share a row or column",
      "all stones share one common row or column",
      "stones connected only through a chain, not directly to each other"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "stones = [[0,0],[0,1],[1,0],[1,2],[2,1],[2,2]]",
        "output": "5",
        "expectedOutput": "5",
        "explanation": "every stone is connected to some other stone through a chain of shared rows/columns, so all but one can be removed"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "stones = [[0,0],[0,2],[1,1],[2,0],[2,2]]",
        "output": "3",
        "expectedOutput": "3",
        "explanation": "four stones form one connected group (leave 1 behind), and the middle stone is alone (leave it too), so 5 - 2 = 3 are removable"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "stones = [[0,0],[1,1]]",
        "output": "0",
        "expectedOutput": "0",
        "explanation": "the two stones share no row or column, so neither can ever be removed"
      }
